 r←ResolveReadmeLinks_ match;m;ind;v;scheme
⍝ Replacement function for `ResolveReadmeLinks`; see there for what is decided and why.
⍝ `group`, `repo` and `tag` are not arguments because ⎕R decides what a replacement function
⍝ is given: they come from the caller, where they are locals.
 m←match.Match
 ind←m⍳'"'
 v←¯1↓ind↓m
 r←m
 :If 0=≢v
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If '#'=⊃v                                         ⍝ Points within this page; already dealt with
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If 0<≢scheme←UrlScheme v
     :If (⊂⎕C scheme)∊'javascript' 'data' 'vbscript'
         r←(ind↑m),'#"'                             ⍝ The one thing a link must not be allowed to do
     :EndIf
     :Return                                        ⍝ Any other scheme: already absolute
 :EndIf
 :If '//'≡2↑v                                       ⍝ Protocol relative: absolute as well
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If 0=≢group                                       ⍝ Nothing to resolve against
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If './'≡2↑v
     v←2↓v
 :EndIf
 :If '/'=⊃v                                         ⍝ Site relative, so GitHub resolves it against github.com itself
     r←(ind↑m),'https://github.com',v,'"'
     :Return
 :EndIf
 :If 'src'≡⎕C(ind-2)↑m
     r←(ind↑m),(GetRawGitHubUrl group repo tag v),'"'
 :Else
     r←(ind↑m),(GetBlobGitHubUrl group repo tag v),'"'
 :EndIf
